---
// Privacy policy (UK GDPR). DRAFT: to be reviewed by the business before launch.
// The cookies section switches automatically: analytics details appear only once a GTM ID is configured.
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = '12 October 2026';
const analytics = site.tracking;
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Eclipse Shield Ltd collects, uses and protects your personal information, including quote requests made through this website."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  intro={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} ("Eclipse Shield", "we", "us") is a window film company based in {site.base}, registered in
    {' '}{site.registeredIn} with company number {site.companyNumber}. We are the data controller for the personal
    information described in this policy.
  </p>
  <p>Contact us about privacy at <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>Quote requests</h3>
  <p>When you use our quote form, we collect the details you choose to give us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, email address, phone number and preferred contact method</li>
    <li>details about the property and windows, what you need, and when</li>
    <li>your postcode and town</li>
    <li>photos of your windows, and any notes you add</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this information to reply to you, prepare a quote, arrange a survey and, if you go ahead, carry out the
    work. Our lawful basis is that you have asked us to take these steps before entering into a contract with us. If you
    become a customer, we keep records needed to provide the service and meet our legal obligations, such as tax and
    accounting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Photos are resized on your device before they are sent, which also removes hidden location data. Please avoid
    including people or personal documents in your photos.
  </p>

  <h3>Emails and phone calls</h3>
  <p>
    If you email or call us, we use your details to answer your enquiry and, if you ask us to, to provide a quote or
    carry out work.
  </p>

  <h3>Spam protection</h3>
  <p>
    Our quote form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check that submissions come from people rather than automated programs.
    Turnstile processes technical information such as your IP address and browser details for this purpose. Our lawful
    basis is our legitimate interest in keeping the form secure and free from spam.
  </p>

  <h3>Website hosting and security</h3>
  <p>
    Our website is hosted by Cloudflare, which processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver pages and protect
    the site from attacks.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

  <h3>Necessary</h3>
  <p>These are needed for the website to work and don’t need your consent:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your cookie choice, saved in your browser’s local storage (<code>es_consent</code>) for 12 months so we don’t ask
      on every page.
    </li>
    <li>Security and spam protection from Cloudflare, including Turnstile on the quote form.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  {
    analytics ? (
      <>
        <p>
          If you allow analytics, we use Google Analytics (through Google Tag Manager) to see which pages are visited,
          how people find us and whether the quote form works well. This tells us about visits in general. We don’t use
          it to identify you, and we don’t use advertising features. Nothing from Google is loaded until you accept.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
              <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
              <th scope="col">Lasts</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga</code></td>
              <td>Tells visits from different browsers apart</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td>
              <td>Keeps track of a visit (session)</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          Our lawful basis is your consent. You can change your mind at any time with the <strong>Cookie settings</strong>
          link at the bottom of every page. If you withdraw consent, we stop analytics and remove these cookies.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        We do not currently use analytics or advertising cookies. If we add them, we will only use them with your
        consent, and we will update this policy first.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Who we share your information with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your information. We use these service providers to run our business:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: website hosting, security and spam protection</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong>: delivers quote requests from the website to our inbox</li>
    <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong>: our business email, where your enquiry is stored</li>
    {analytics && <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong>: website statistics, only if you allow analytics cookies</li>}
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers act on our instructions. Some may process data outside the UK. Where they do, we rely on safeguards
    recognised under UK data protection law, such as the UK–US Data Bridge or standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiries that don’t lead to work: deleted within 12 months of our last contact.</li>
    <li>Customer records: kept for 6 years after the job, to meet tax and accounting requirements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The website itself does not store quote requests. They are sent straight to our email.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the information we hold about you</li>
    <li>ask us to correct or delete it</li>
    <li>object to or restrict how we use it</li>
    <li>ask us to transfer it to you or another organisation, where this applies</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a> to use any of these rights. We will reply within one month. If you are unhappy
    with how we handle your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this page if anything changes. The date at the top shows when it was last updated.</p>
</PageLayout>
